{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FreeModule.Finite.Matrix","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Perm","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.IdentityIContentDecomposition"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.spectralData_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.spectralData_zero","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L174-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.identityB_content_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.identityB_content_form","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L146-L164","doc":"**Identity (B) in literal content form, conditional (Layer 2).** Reading off each block `i` as a\npartition `κ i` whose dimension is the Frame–Robinson–Thrall hook-length value `dimHLF (κ i)` and\nwhose Jucys–Murphy eigenvalue is the content-square sum `sumSqContents (κ i) = Σ_{c∈κ i} c(c)²`\n(the two identifications that the assumed Wedderburn/JM bundle supplies), `identityB_conditional`\nbecomes the **literal Plancherel content-square mean**\n`Σ_i dim(κ i)²·(Σ_{c∈κ i} c²) = n!·binom(n,2)`. This is the **general-`n`** counterpart of the\nsibling's bounded check `IdentityI.idB_verified_le12` (`n ≤ 12`): the same per-partition summand\n`dimHLF² · sumSqContents` (cf. `IdentityI.identityB_lhs`), now an identity for all `n` modulo the\nsingle Wedderburn/JM hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.identityB_conditional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.identityB_conditional","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L135-L143","doc":"**Identity (B), conditional on the Wedderburn/JM block spectral decomposition.**\n`Σ_i dim(λ_i)²·ω_i = n!·binom(n,2)`, obtained by equating **side 2** (`blockTrace_eq`) with\n**side 1** (`RegularRepTrace.trace_centralC2_eq_factorial_mul_choose_two`, proved unconditionally\nover any `CommRing`). Reading `ω_i = Σ_{c∈λ_i} c(c)²` (the JM eigenvalue) makes this the literal\nPlancherel content-square mean carried by the keystone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.sumSq_dim_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.sumSq_dim_eq","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L119-L133","doc":"**RSK sum-of-squares, conditional.** `Σ_i dim(λ_i)² = n!` — the \"dimension side\" the\n`Δ_λ`-gate note flagged as needing HLF/RSK. Produced from completeness `Σ_i proj_i = id`,\n`tr(id) = finrank = |S_n| = n!`, and `tr(proj_i) = dim(λ_i)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.blockTrace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.blockTrace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L105-L117","doc":"**Side 2 of the Identity-(B) trace equation.** Given a Wedderburn/JM block spectral\ndecomposition, the trace of `mulLeft C₂` on the regular representation is `Σ_i ω_i · dim(λ_i)²`.\nThe `dim(λ_i)²` weighting is *produced* by `LinearMap.IsProj.trace` (the trace of the block\nprojection equals the rank `d i ^ 2` of its range), not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.complete","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L99-L99","doc":"The blocks exhaust the regular representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.decomp","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L97-L97","doc":"**Block spectral decomposition**: `C₂` acts as the scalar `ω i` on block `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.rank","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L95-L95","doc":"The `i`-th isotypic block has R-dimension `dim(λ_i)²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.isProj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.isProj","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L93-L93","doc":"`proj i` is the projection onto `p i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.proj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.proj","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L91-L91","doc":"The projection onto block `i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.p","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L89-L89","doc":"The `i`-th isotypic block (R-dimension `d i ^ 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.ω","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.ω","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L87-L87","doc":"`ω i` = the scalar by which `C₂` acts on block `i` (the JM eigenvalue `Σ_{c∈λ_i} c(c)²`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.d","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L85-L85","doc":"`d i = dim(λ_i)`, the dimension of the `i`-th irreducible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.fintypeIdx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.fintypeIdx","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.Idx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.Idx","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L82-L82","doc":"Index of the irreducible blocks (the partitions of `n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L80-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepBlockTrace.SnWedderburnSpectralData","kind":"structure","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepBlockTrace.lean#L70-L99","doc":"**The isolated Mathlib gap for side 2.** A Wedderburn / Jucys–Murphy *block spectral\ndecomposition* of `mulLeft C₂` on the regular representation `R[S_n]`: a finite family of\nprojections `proj i` onto blocks `p i` of R-dimension `d i ^ 2` (the `λ`-isotypic components,\n`dim(λ)²`), the central element acting as the scalar `ω i` on block `i`\n(`mulLeft C₂ = Σ_i ω_i · proj_i`), and the blocks exhausting the space (`Σ_i proj_i = id`).\n\nThis bundles precisely the **S_n Okounkov–Vershik content not in Mathlib** (the partition ↔\nirreducible classification, `dim(λ) = #SYT(λ)`, and JM eigenvalues = contents) that pins the blocks\nand scalars; the *existence* of such a decomposition is semisimplicity (`RepresentationTheory.Maschke`,\nwhich is in Mathlib). Every theorem below is proved outright *given* such a datum. ","signatureChunk":0}]}